                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "cd0b01e8-b45e-3449-a7c6-1c84b0553e65",
                        "entry_id": "e09024f9-798f-3cd6-a704-aeafd4726317",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A partly sheltered anchorage; a stretch of water near the shore where vessels may ride at anchor, but with less protection than a harbour."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "dd035bc3-42d8-4fdc-a2c5-705fb9a68c47",
                                "sense_id": "cd0b01e8-b45e-3449-a7c6-1c84b0553e65",
                                "text": "In 1620 junks began to arrive from China depositing hundreds of migrants, and with the resumption of China's official trade to Southeast Asia in 1683, the numbers of junks arriving annually in Batavia's roadstead grew from an average of three or four to about twenty."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "1c006972-4502-45f0-b2aa-28d66125d67c",
                                "sense_id": "cd0b01e8-b45e-3449-a7c6-1c84b0553e65",
                                "text": "The shores of Protection island form on its south side, which is about two miles long, a most excellent roadstead, and a channel into port Discovery, near 2 miles wide on either side […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "9ab3cb0c-de2b-4e3f-b539-7d17db883ee5",
                                "sense_id": "cd0b01e8-b45e-3449-a7c6-1c84b0553e65",
                                "text": "[…] I found we were lying in a roadstead among many low and rocky islets, hovered about by an innumerable cloud of sea-fowl."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "259d37f4-e7cd-43e3-9d41-78e385ff7be2",
                                "sense_id": "cd0b01e8-b45e-3449-a7c6-1c84b0553e65",
                                "text": "[…] that was the time when at the mast-heads of the three-deckers and seventy-fours moored in her own roadstead […] the blue-jackets, to be numbered by thousands, ran up with huzzas the British colors with the union and cross wiped out […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e9b8c5e5-707e-4d22-b809-ecebf0b59ed2",
                                "sense_id": "cd0b01e8-b45e-3449-a7c6-1c84b0553e65",
                                "text": "Clusters of strong flowers rose everywhere above the coarse tussocks of bent. It was like a roadstead crowded with tall fairy-shipping."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "fb298652-f969-49a7-8cbc-040352ec9d01",
                        "source_entry_id": "e09024f9-798f-3cd6-a704-aeafd4726317",
                        "source_sense_id": "cd0b01e8-b45e-3449-a7c6-1c84b0553e65",
